## Putting nginx in front

An app that binds to `127.0.0.1` (the pattern used by `splam` in [Install Apps](install-apps.qmd) and daemonized in [Lab 10](lab10.qmd)) isn't reachable from outside its own instance. Something has to accept the connection on `443`, terminate TLS, and forward the request inward.

Install `nginx`:


::: {.cell}

```{.bash .cell-code  code-fold="false"}
sudo amazon-linux-extras install -y nginx1
```
:::


Create the site configuration:


::: {.cell}

```{.bash .cell-code  code-fold="false"}
sudo vim /etc/nginx/conf.d/splam.conf
```
:::



```{.default}
server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name splam.example.com;

    ssl_certificate     /etc/letsencrypt/live/splam.example.com/fullchain.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/splam.example.com/privkey.pem;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
    }
}
```

The certificate paths assume you have a hostname pointed at the instance, covered in [Configure DNS](configure-dns.qmd).

Test the configuration before reloading, since a syntax error will otherwise take `nginx` down entirely:


::: {.cell}

```{.bash .cell-code  code-fold="false"}
sudo nginx -t
```
:::



```{.default}
nginx: the configuration file /etc/nginx/nginx.conf syntax is ok
nginx: configuration file /etc/nginx/nginx.conf test is successful
```

Then enable and start it, the same two step pattern as the app itself:


::: {.cell}

```{.bash .cell-code  code-fold="false"}
sudo systemctl enable --now nginx
```
:::



